# Weakens H's CloseHeadMonotone in this module's environment: a close overwrites
# the heads L's marker requires instead of max-merging with them. A window opened
# after the purge and before the re-created incarnation's first initialisation
# closes after it with heads below the straddler, so the initialisation's heads are
# lost and the re-created incarnation's live advance passes the straddler.
# Production max-merges in HandOffMarkerCore.RequiredHead.
MODULE: ReadPositionHonestAssumeCloseReplacesHeads
TARGET: ReadPositionHonest
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a close overwrites the heads earlier closes and the initialisation recorded
PERTURBS: Close
BOUNDS: WithRecreate = TRUE, WithUnclaimedSurvivor = FALSE, WithPreArm = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ \E h \in IF mInit THEN HeadsAbove(CloseCovers) ELSE 0..next : hoClosedAt' = Max2(hoClosedAt, h)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the close overwrites the recorded heads.
    /\ \E h \in IF mInit THEN HeadsAbove(CloseCovers) ELSE 0..next : hoClosedAt' = h
--- END
